From 14abd53ac70e6a58de15f4bba42b192285c35679 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 18:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] perf(spec-decode): vocabulary-parallel greedy DSpark drafts

Greedy DSpark drafting all-gathers the full-vocabulary draft logits, and
every rank reads the whole replicated Markov projection (129280 x 256
bf16, 66 MB) once per draft position: about 330 MB per step at five
drafts, most of the drafter's time at one stream.

With SPARK3_DSPARK_VOCAB_PARALLEL=1 the Markov projection is sharded by
vocabulary rows like the LM head. Each rank reduces base logits plus
Markov bias over its own shard to a (max, global index) pair in the same
fused kernel, the pairs are all-gathered (8 bytes per request and rank),
and a small kernel keeps the first maximum. Shards hold ascending index
ranges, so ties and NaNs resolve as in the full-vocabulary argmax and the
drafts are unchanged; the target verifies every token as before. Greedy
drafting over the full target vocabulary only; other paths are untouched.
Off by default.
